		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2009#p2009"><![CDATA[
It is a matter of interpretation, and you get what you put into the system, but if you use default gravity of -9.8 m^2/sec, indeed 1 meter equals 1 unit, and 1 timeStep unit equals 1 second.<br><br>The tuning parameters (collision margin, timestep size, contact breaking treshold etc) have been tuned with those settings in mind.<br><br>You can also interpret the values in other units (aside from the tuning parameters, Bullet is unit-free).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Sun Oct 01, 2006 5:55 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
